## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests scanned · 8 Critical · 1 High · 1 Medium · 0 Low**

This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called — yielding ~95% line coverage — but almost nothing is actually *verified*. A bug in any method except perhaps `GetProduct` (which still only checks `!= null`) would go undetected.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests giving false confidence

#### 1. Systematic coverage-touching (suite-wide)

The entire class methodically calls every public member on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order with no meaningful assertions. This is the single root cause of "95% coverage but production bugs."

**Affected tests (no assertions at all):**

| # | Test method | Line |
|---|-----------|------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` | 17 |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | 32 |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39 |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` | 63 |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69 |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 84 |

**Fix — example for `AddProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 17-21) — no assertion
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER — verify the product was persisted
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
```

**Fix — `UpdatePrice_Works`:**
```csharp
// AFTER — verify price actually changed
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")?.Price);
```

**Fix — `RemoveProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
// AFTER — verify product is gone
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**Fix — `GetProductCount_Works`:**
```csharp
// AFTER — verify the count
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**Fix — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`:**
```csharp
// AFTER — verify discounted prices
